# Product requirements

> Requirements describe what must be true for users and stakeholders. Keep implementation choices
> in architecture notes, feature specs, and ADRs.

## Core obligations

1. [Observable user-facing capability or outcome.]
2. [Reliability, safety, privacy, accessibility, or quality obligation.]
3. [Explanation, control, or feedback obligation where relevant.]

## Guardrails

1. [A harmful or misleading behavior the system must prevent.]
2. [A boundary on automated action, cost, data use, or operational risk.]
3. [A condition under which the system must degrade safely or pause.]

## Release and evidence gates

1. [Evidence required before a material behavior becomes active.]
2. [Required owner review or approval for an irreversible or high-impact change.]
3. [Required rollback, observation, or support condition.]

## Non-requirements

- [Capability intentionally deferred or explicitly not promised.]
- [Unsupported integration, audience, environment, or automation level.]

